<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Brief, 4x4 - the horizon.

  GENERATED SHAPE, HAND-OWNED CONTENT. All three brief layouts carry the
  identical row block — bar, kind icon, title, text, mark — so a row looks
  the same at every size and the provider can bind any of them with one
  piece of code. tools/check_widget_wiring.py counts the row ids here and
  compares them with BriefRender.ROWS_4X4; if they disagree the widget
  silently drops items, which is the v0.9.0 bug.

  NOTHING HERE ROTATES. Earlier versions paged through the brief and showed
  "1/2" in the footer, which meant the row you came to check might not be on
  screen when you looked. The rows are now ordered by urgency and fixed, and
  the footer names what is below the fold instead of numbering pages.

  Every colour is a resource reference, never a literal, so the LAUNCHER
  resolves it: that is what makes values-night and the Material You palette
  in values-v31 work on a home screen. The provider only ever sends resource
  ids and strings.
-->
<LinearLayout xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:id="@+id/widgetRoot"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:orientation="vertical"
    android:background="@drawable/bg_widget"
